  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Content types",
      "text": "Use `<Card.Body>` to pad content inside a `<Card>`.\n\nAlternatively, you can use this shorthand version for Cards with body\nonly, and no other children\n\nUsing `<Card.Title>`, `<Card.Subtitle>`, and\n`<Card.Text>` inside the `<Card.Body>` will line them up nicely.\n`<Card.Link>`s are used to line up links next to each other.\n\n`<Card.Text>` outputs `<p>` tags around the content, so you can\nuse multiple `<Card.Text>`s to create separate paragraphs.\n\nCreate lists of content in a card with a flush list group.\n\nYou may add a header by adding a `<Card.Header>` component.\n\nA `<CardHeader>` can be styled by passing a heading element\nthrough the `<as>` prop",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Images",
      "text": "Cards include a few options for working with images. Choose from\nappending “image caps” at either end of a card, overlaying images with\ncard content, or simply embedding the image in a card.\n\nSimilar to headers and footers, cards can include top and bottom “image\ncaps”—images at the top or bottom of a card.\n\nTurn an image into a card background and overlay your card’s text.\nDepending on the image, you may or may not need additional styles or\nutilities.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Navigation",
      "text": "Add some navigation to a card’s header (or block) with React Bootstrap’s\n[Nav](navs) components.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Card Styles",
      "text": "You can change a card's appearance by changing their `<bg>`, and `<text>` props.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Card layout",
      "text": "Use `Row`'s [grid column](../layout/grid#setting-column-widths-in-row) props to control how many cards to show per row.",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
